Public finance, collective provision, and commons (@public-finance-collective-provision-and-commons: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_2EE3Y6NDNF2VNYQEW6AZCJNZ09
This material investigates how communities organise taxation, expenditure, public services, shared resources, and collective investment. It connects budgets, provision, ownership, cooperation, incentives, distribution, and political decisions with the institutions that maintain common capabilities over time. Study a defined service or resource through its financing, operation, effects, and competing arrangements. Link water, energy, knowledge, and infrastructure examples to the relevant economic models and social evidence while making evaluative choices visible.

**Parent:** [Political-Economy](../Political-Economy.lingua#r_2WPG1Y767BM24Z0K4BY6Y6T62W).
